  "step_3": "First, the information relevant to the decision reason includes the outcomes, their probabilities, and the reference value (0). The individual did not consider the outcomes (3000 vs. 6000) or compute differences from the reference value. They only focused on the probabilities. Second, the decision reason’s rule is to prefer the lottery with the higher mean difference (i.e., expected value of outcome minus reference value), which is equivalent to expected value in this case (since reference value is 0). The individual’s justification is based solely on selecting the higher probability, not on expected value or mean difference. Although both lotteries have the same expected value (6 Euros), the individual chose based on probability alone, which is a different criterion. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason. The reason was not applied in the deliberation process.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
